{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1382583-tepet-chars-and-futile-blood-location","id":1382583,"title":"Tepet chars and Futile Blood location","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-19T13:21:36-07:00","id":1382583,"title":"Tepet chars and Futile Blood location","content":"I'd been thinking about a Tepet dynast character who as a short term goal wants to recover their dead mother's armor from the Battle of Futile Blood. I thought it could make a cool start for a grand tour for some dynasts who head north to south east. But I'm actually not sure where in the north the battle took place except near Fallen Lapis which I also don't know the location of, especially with the north's geographic changes in 3e. Anyone with superior exalted knowlegde know, or have a general idea?<br /> <br /> Also, I was wondering if you all thought t made sense for a newly graduated Tepet to do the grand tour thing, especially one with a martial education. The dragonblood book suggests the houses in general are keeping those scions close, nevermind Tepet. If that doesn't make sense, how would you get a Tepet character into a &quot;usual&quot; DB group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:45:10-07:00","id":1382589,"title":"","content":"Well, I think we can assume it's north of the White Sea, but I'm mostly posting to express my support for that character motivation. It's a cool idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1382583-tepet-chars-and-futile-blood-location#post1382583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that doesn't make sense, how would you get a Tepet character into a &quot;usual&quot; DB group?</div> </div> </div> </div> While I do think it makes sense (why would they include the grand tour if not to suggest PCs do it?), DBs always have the excuse of being wilful elemental demigods. If it can get you a love match in defiance of longstanding marriage arrangements, it can get you a colonial adventure and a chance to retrieve an ancestral artifact.<br /> <br /> As a Tepet, your character gets an additional excuse in the form of their warrior's code (<b>the Realm</b>, p. 67), which could put quite a bit of weight behind the desire to reclaim their mother's legacy (not to mention the House's property).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:57:10-07:00","id":1382636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I think we can assume it's north of the White Sea </div> </div> </div> That doesn't make much sense. Though would make recovering it a bit cooler...<br /> <br /> <br /> In 2nd, I believe the battle was south-east of Linowan (which doesn't make a lot of sense. But a wizard did it. A zenith wizard).<br /> <br /> So, essentially Tumbleweed, you see the river that goes around Medo and up to a big bay and into the White Sea? The Bull's Empire is around there. So somewhere east of Whitewall, north of Medo, north of Pneuma, west of Rubylak. So presumably the battle was in that area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T05:15:22-07:00","id":1382717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, don't think we know precisely in 3e, or if we ever did exactly. In 2e, Fallen Lapis (wiped out by the Bronze Faction) is mentioned just before the battle of Futile Blood as throwing in their lot with the Bull, and that was directly north of Mount Metagalapa and Greyfalls \u2013 only slightly more than the distance between Lookshy and Great Forks. That whole campaign's geography and logistics weren't... brilliant... but as Wizard says, magic.<br /> <br /> Completely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a>, it's a great idea for a campaign. Can see elders agreeing that 'such a treasured artefact must be returned to us for Tepet to reclaim our honour', and then who knows what debts of honour or leads the hearthmates will rack up during the search that require immediate attention and delay hurrying home \u2013 'V'Neef Super Archer saved my life from that icewalker anathema, but has been left badly wounded in the process, honour demands I take him to Whitewall for immediate medical attention.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-20-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}